//@version=6
strategy("W5 MR revival global placed held", overlay=true, initial_capital=10000, default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100, margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

// Lane W5-ENG-MARGIN-V6, mechanism MR (revival). The shape of lab tv tape
// badapter-v19dp1-control (NYSE:F 15, R5 lane B-ADAPTER): a 940-share short
// with a stop exit X; a long + strategy.close pair on 04-30 15:45 ET that the
// 05-01 open declines; a margin call on 05-02 09:30. Here X is placed
// on 04-30 10:00 while short, from_entry="". Does the margin call revive it and close through it?
t(m, d, h, mi) => timestamp("America/New_York", 2025, m, d, h, mi)
if time == t(4, 29, 15, 45)
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty=940)
if time == t(4, 30, 10, 0)
    strategy.exit("X", "", stop=10.25)
if time == t(4, 30, 15, 45)
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    strategy.close("S", comment="Reverse to Long")
